<article class="env-definition" id="0GGE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GGE">Definition <span data-tag="0GGE">88.14.7</span>.</a> Let $A$ be an adic topological ring which has a finitely generated ideal of definition. Let $f \in A$. The <em>completed principal localization</em> $A_{\{ f\} }$ of $A$ is the completion of $A_ f = A[1/f]$ of the principal localization of $A$ at $f$ with respect to any ideal of definition of $A$. </p>
